# Error contract

Public failures are generated `api.v1.Error` (`scheda::Error`). Not anyhow.
Bindings and agent JSON use the Protobuf JSON mapping (`08`). Callers branch on
`code`, not `message` or `stack`.

Follow `.cursor/skills/error-handling/SKILL.md` when adding `Error.Code` values,
constructing errors, or converting `map_err` / `format!(...: {err})` sites.

## Fields

- **`code`**: class of the **root** reason (deep cause), not the LIB-2 method
  name. Honest enums only — no catch-all `CODE_IO` / `CODE_GIT`. Schema rule
  text stays in `message` under `CODE_INVALID`.
- **`message`**: must not replace `code`.
- **`path`**: vault-relative POSIX of the file this failure is about. Unset
  when there is no such file (remote network, ANN dump under `.scheda/`).
- **`repeat`**: constructors set it from `default_repeat(code)`. Override with
  `with_repeat` when the **method** knows better.
- **`stack`**: causal frames, **outermost first**. Not a language backtrace.
  Must not repeat `path` and must not replace `code`. No crate/module prefix
  (`ann.AnnIndex` is wrong).

## Rust bubbling

- Already `Result<T, Error>`: `.context(frame)` (literal); `.with_context(|| …)` (lazy).
- `std::io::Error`: `.context(frame)` (`ContextIo`, maps via `io_code`).
- git CLI (exit + stderr): `git_code`, then `.context(frame)`.
- Other foreign `Display` (`usearch`, tantivy, serde): `.context(Code::…, frame)`.
- Interpolated frames: `.with_context(|| format!("… {n}"))` (only on `Err`).
- Leaf constructors: inherent on generated `Error` (`Error::invalid`, `Error::io_not_found`, …).
- `ensure!` / `bail!` for our `Error`. After proto edits:
  `bazel run //api/v1:generate`.
